{"id": "96dadaa7bd2b53b888044ccba442af4d", "ts": "1775655120.000000", "text": "You should treat TX as active for Q1. Acme crossed $612K trailing-12 Texas sales, so economic nexus was already met. That means TX is not $0 and you need destination-based local calculation by ZIP, not a single blended state rate.

I checked the sales rollforward before replying. Please rerun TX on the per-ZIP local rates and update the thread total from there.

One more correction on the prior breakdown: GA, NC, CA, FL, and IL should all be $0 for Acme. Their SaaS revenue is not subject to sales tax in those states (services exempt or SaaS specifically carved out), so no filings are required this quarter. The old CA-only standing monthly entries were reclassified after the prior-period review, so there is no $29K sitting in 225000 from earlier months. Treat the full Q1 liability as a new incremental accrual.", "type": "message", "subtype": null, "user_id": "persona_004", "channel_id": "C006", "created_at": "2026-04-08T13:32:00+00:00", "files_json": "[]", "reply_count": 0, "latest_reply": null, "reactions_json": "[]", "attachments_json": "[]", "thread_parent_id": null, "thread_ts_legacy": null, "reply_users_count": 0, "is_activity_message": false}
